    "type": "question",
    "label": "49",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equation.\n$$9^x-4(3^{x+1})+27=0.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=1$ or $x=2$.\n\nLet $u=3^x$, using $9^x=u^2$ and $3^{x+1}=3u$.",
      "worked": "Let $u=3^x>0$. Then $9^x=u^2$ and $3^{x+1}=3u$.\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2-12u+27&=0\\\\(u-3)(u-9)&=0\\\\u&=3\\text{ or }u=9\\\\3^x&=3^1\\text{ or }3^x=3^2\\\\x&=1\\text{ or }x=2.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
